{
  "duration": 204.8464375,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 2.28,
      "text": "You've put in the time to learn the mechanics."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.9,
      "end": 8.22,
      "text": "You now know how to use AI, and you understand the engine underneath, which means its strange"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.22,
      "end": 10.1,
      "text": "behavior finally makes sense."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.92,
      "end": 12.84,
      "text": "You've achieved the core goal of this course."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.38,
      "end": 15.1,
      "text": "You are now smarter than the tool."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.2,
      "end": 20.38,
      "text": "So that brings us to the question almost everyone is arguing about right now."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.02,
      "end": 22.44,
      "text": "Where does all this actually land?"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.34,
      "end": 27.66,
      "text": "Moving from understanding how a piece of software functions to projecting its impact"
    },
    {
      "start": 27.66,
      "end": 29.94,
      "text": "on society is a massive leap."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.56,
      "end": 34.84,
      "text": "We are leaving the realm of factual certainty and entering a space of wild speculation."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.6,
      "end": 37.22,
      "text": "You've definitely heard the voices already."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.82,
      "end": 43.3,
      "text": "You probably know an AI optimist who thinks this technology is amazing, fantastic, and"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.3,
      "end": 45.66,
      "text": "worthy of every other superlative they can string together."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.22,
      "end": 50.52,
      "text": "And you know an AI warrior who is absolutely certain it's going to hurt society."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.42,
      "end": 52.22,
      "text": "Here's the honest part."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.96,
      "end": 53.84,
      "text": "Nobody knows."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.56,
      "end": 55.04,
      "text": "Not them."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.46,
      "end": 55.86,
      "text": "Not us."
    },
    {
      "start": 55.86,
      "end": 57.74,
      "text": "Not the people building AI."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.78,
      "end": 62.94,
      "text": "Being an expert at coding neural networks does not grant the ability to predict human history."
    },
    {
      "start": 63.64,
      "end": 68.46,
      "text": "Because technical expertise does not equal prophetic vision, both the utopian promises"
    },
    {
      "start": 68.46,
      "end": 71.64,
      "text": "and the doomsday warnings you hear are ultimately just guesses."
    },
    {
      "start": 72.9,
      "end": 74.1,
      "text": "Think back to history class."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.96,
      "end": 78.9,
      "text": "Centuries ago, mapmakers had to figure out what to do with vast stretches of ocean"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.9,
      "end": 80.28,
      "text": "they simply did not understand."
    },
    {
      "start": 80.84,
      "end": 85.6,
      "text": "Their solution was to fill those uncharted waters with imagined sea monsters and strange"
    },
    {
      "start": 85.6,
      "end": 86.06,
      "text": "serpents."
    },
    {
      "start": 86.74,
      "end": 92.02,
      "text": "The future of AI is exactly like the unknown parts of the ocean on those old maps."
    },
    {
      "start": 92.76,
      "end": 96.6,
      "text": "The AI warriors look out at that blank space and draw modern monsters."
    },
    {
      "start": 97.26,
      "end": 101.82,
      "text": "They picture a technology that destroys jobs, hacks systems, and takes over the world."
    },
    {
      "start": 102.88,
      "end": 108.5,
      "text": "Meanwhile, AI optimists stare at the exact same unknown waters and see only easy, clear"
    },
    {
      "start": 108.5,
      "end": 110.04,
      "text": "sailing through open channels."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.04,
      "end": 116.2,
      "text": "Both extreme optimism and extreme dread are just the human mind drawing sea monsters to"
    },
    {
      "start": 116.2,
      "end": 118.2,
      "text": "cope with the anxiety of an empty map."
    },
    {
      "start": 119.1,
      "end": 122.76,
      "text": "But look at what those early sailors actually found when they pushed past the edge."
    },
    {
      "start": 123.22,
      "end": 124.38,
      "text": "They didn't run into sea monsters."
    },
    {
      "start": 124.82,
      "end": 127.02,
      "text": "And they very rarely got easy, clear sailing."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.76,
      "end": 130.76,
      "text": "What they usually encountered was something completely unexpected."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.9,
      "end": 135.28,
      "text": "Throughout this section, we are going to take both views of our map seriously."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.28,
      "end": 139.9,
      "text": "The very real risks of the monsters and the genuine benefits of the open water."
    },
    {
      "start": 140.6,
      "end": 144.14,
      "text": "As we do, only one thing is certain, AI is here to stay."
    },
    {
      "start": 144.92,
      "end": 146.72,
      "text": "That doesn't mean it keeps getting better forever."
    },
    {
      "start": 147.18,
      "end": 149.24,
      "text": "Just that the technology isn't going away."
    },
    {
      "start": 150.1,
      "end": 153.44,
      "text": "Navigating successfully doesn't require predicting the future perfectly."
    },
    {
      "start": 153.88,
      "end": 158.44,
      "text": "It requires accepting the permanence of the technology and staying agile enough to handle"
    },
    {
      "start": 158.44,
      "end": 160.58,
      "text": "the reality of whatever actually emerges."
    },
    {
      "start": 161.4,
      "end": 166.56,
      "text": "This chart outlines the framework we will use for this section, built around three guiding questions."
    },
    {
      "start": 167.28,
      "end": 170.5,
      "text": "One, why do people disagree so much about AI's future?"
    },
    {
      "start": 171.2,
      "end": 173.84,
      "text": "Two, what could AI do to make society better?"
    },
    {
      "start": 174.28,
      "end": 175.54,
      "text": "And where could it go wrong?"
    },
    {
      "start": 176.22,
      "end": 180.3,
      "text": "And three, how could AI change my future life and work?"
    },
    {
      "start": 181.24,
      "end": 186.78,
      "text": "Focusing on these specific inquiries arms us with a compass rather than a predetermined map."
    },
    {
      "start": 187.22,
      "end": 191.0,
      "text": "The destination ahead of us is still entirely unmapped."
    },
    {
      "start": 191.52,
      "end": 192.88,
      "text": "Nobody has a map of what's coming."
    },
    {
      "start": 193.52,
      "end": 195.44,
      "text": "You're ready to sail into the blank space."
    },
    {
      "start": 196.34,
      "end": 201.24,
      "text": "Navigating the future requires stepping into the unknown with readiness rather than fear."
    }
  ],
